sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    
    box User Space
    participant App as User App
    end
    
    box Linux Kernel Space
    participant VFS as VFS (File System)
    participant PCI as PCI Subsystem
    participant Driver as vGPU Driver
    end
    
    box Motherboard
    participant RAM as System RAM (Host)
    participant PCIe as PCIe Bus (Motherboard)
    end
    
    box FPGA
    participant XDMA as XDMA IP (Endpoint)
    participant AXI as AXI Interconnect
    participant vGPU_IP as Custom vGPU IP
    end

    %% Phase 1: Boot & Driver Load
    Note over App, vGPU_IP: [1] Boot & Driver Initialization
    PCI->>PCIe: PCIe Bus Enumeration (BIOS/Kernel boot)
    PCIe-->>PCI: Discover FPGA (Vendor ID: 0x10EE)
    Note over PCI, PCIe: PCIe Configuration (BAR Sizing & Allocation)
    PCI->>PCI: Assign Physical Address space for BAR0
    PCI->>XDMA: PCIe Config Write: Write Physical Addr back to BAR0
    
    Driver->>PCI: module_init() -> pci_register_driver()
    PCI->>Driver: Match ID -> vgpu_probe(pdev)
    
    Driver->>PCI: pci_enable_device(), pci_request_regions()
    Driver->>PCI: pci_ioremap_bar(pdev, 0)
    PCI-->>Driver: Returns mmio_base (Virtual Addr mapped to BAR0)
    
    Driver->>PCI: pci_alloc_irq_vectors() (Request MSI/MSI-X)
    Driver->>PCI: request_irq(dev->irq, vgpu_irq_handler)
    
    Driver->>RAM: dma_alloc_coherent() (Allocate Consistent Ring Buffer)
    RAM-->>Driver: Return Virtual Addr (CPU) & Bus Addr (FPGA)
    Note over Driver, XDMA: Provide FPGA with the Ring Buffer Base Address
    Driver->>XDMA: iowrite64(dma_handle, mmio_base + 0x0C)
    
    Driver->>RAM: __get_free_pages() (Allocate Cached Payload Buffer)
    Driver->>Driver: dma_map_single() (Streaming DMA Mapping)
    Note over Driver, XDMA: Provide FPGA with the Payload Base Address
    Driver->>XDMA: iowrite64(payload_dma_handle, mmio_base + 0x14)
    
    Driver->>VFS: cdev_add(), device_create(/dev/vgpu0)

    %% Phase 2: User Initialization
    Note over App, vGPU_IP: [2] Application Initialization
    App->>VFS: open("/dev/vgpu0")
    VFS->>Driver: vgpu_open() (Allocates vgpu_context)
    Driver-->>App: File Descriptor (fd)
    
    App->>VFS: mmap(fd, size, offset=0)
    VFS->>Driver: vgpu_mmap(pgoff=0)
    Driver->>Driver: dma_mmap_coherent() (Map Ring Buffer)
    Driver-->>App: Return Ring Buffer Virtual Address
    
    App->>VFS: mmap(fd, size, offset=PAGE_SIZE)
    VFS->>Driver: vgpu_mmap(pgoff=1)
    Driver->>Driver: remap_pfn_range() (Map Cached Payload Buffer)
    Driver-->>App: Return Payload Virtual Address

    %% Phase 3: Command Submission & Doorbell (PCIe + AXI)
    Note over App, vGPU_IP: [3] Command Submission (Lock-Free) & HW Doorbell
    Note over App: CPU Producer: Check if Queue is Full
    App->>RAM: smp_load_acquire(&ring->head) (Read FPGA's head safely)
    
    App->>RAM: Write Command Data to ring->cmds[tail] (Zero-copy)
    
    Note over App: CPU Producer: Update Tail with Memory Barrier
    App->>RAM: smp_store_release(&ring->tail) (Ensure command is committed before tail updates!)
    
    App->>VFS: ioctl(fd, VGPU_IOC_DOORBELL)
    VFS->>Driver: vgpu_ioctl()
    
    Note over Driver: Clear irq_fired = 0 (Prevent Lost Wakeup)
    
    Note over Driver, RAM: Streaming DMA: Cache Flush
    Driver->>RAM: dma_sync_single_for_device() (Flush CPU L1/L2 Cache to Physical RAM)
    
    Note over Driver, PCIe: iowrite32(1, mmio_base + 0x00)
    Driver->>PCIe: Issue Memory Write TLP (Target: BAR0 + 0x00)
    
    Driver->>Driver: wait_event_interruptible()
    Note over App, Driver: Thread goes to SLEEP (Context Switch)

    PCIe->>XDMA: Deliver TLP to FPGA Endpoint
    
    Note over XDMA, AXI: PCIe-to-AXI Translation
    XDMA->>AXI: AXI-Lite Write (Addr: 0x4000_0040)
    AXI->>vGPU_IP: Route to Custom IP (Offset: slv_reg16)
    
    Note over vGPU_IP: Hardware FSM starts processing!

    %% Phase 4: FPGA DMA & Interrupt
    Note over App, vGPU_IP: [4] Hardware Execution & MSI Interrupt
    
    Note over vGPU_IP, PCIe: FPGA Consumer: Read Command
    vGPU_IP->>XDMA: DMA Read Request (Fetch cmds[head])
    XDMA->>PCIe: Memory Read TLP (Host RAM)
    PCIe->>RAM: Direct Memory Access (DMA Read)
    RAM-->>PCIe: Return Command Data Payload
    PCIe-->>XDMA: Memory Read Completion (Data)
    
    vGPU_IP->>vGPU_IP: GPU/AI Compute...
    
    Note over vGPU_IP, PCIe: FPGA Consumer: Write Results & Update Head
    vGPU_IP->>XDMA: DMA Write Request (Write results back)
    vGPU_IP->>XDMA: DMA Write Request (Update ring->head)
    XDMA->>PCIe: Memory Write TLP
    PCIe->>RAM: Direct Memory Access (DMA Write data & new head)
    
    Note over vGPU_IP: Compute Done! Assert usr_irq
    vGPU_IP->>XDMA: Assert Interrupt wire
    XDMA->>PCIe: Issue MSI Memory Write TLP (to CPU APIC)
    
    PCIe->>PCI: CPU receives MSI Interrupt
    PCI->>Driver: Execute Top-Half: vgpu_irq_handler()
    
    Note over Driver, PCIe: Acknowledge Hardware
    Driver->>PCIe: ioread32(mmio_base + 0x44) (Read Status)
    Driver->>PCIe: iowrite32(status, mmio_base + 0x48) (ACK)
    PCIe->>XDMA: TLP to clear FPGA interrupt
    
    Note over Driver: Wake up Application
    Driver->>Driver: wake_up_interruptible(wait_q)
    Driver-->>PCI: return IRQ_HANDLED (Exit Interrupt Context)
    
    Note over Driver: Wakes up from wait_event_interruptible
    Note over Driver, RAM: Streaming DMA: Cache Invalidate
    Driver->>RAM: dma_sync_single_for_cpu() (Invalidate CPU L1/L2 Cache)
    
    Driver-->>App: VGPU_IOC_DOORBELL returns
    Note over App: Thread WAKES UP. Results are ready in memory!
